---
title: Icons
layout: wide
description: Each icon is a partial holding one inline SVG that takes the text colour and sizes to the font-size around it. No sprite, no icon font, no request.
eyebrow: Component
source: partials/icons/ — generated by scripts/vendor.mjs
---
<section class="im-section im-wrap-wide">
	<div class="im-icon-grid">
		{{#each icons}}<div class="im-icon-cell">{{icon this}}<span>{{this}}</span></div>{{/each}}
	</div>
</section>

<section class="im-section im-wrap-wide">
	<h2 class="im-section-title">Using one</h2>
	<div class="im-prose">
		{{{{code}}}}
{{> "icons/search"}}                          ← in a Ghost template
<span class="text-accent text-h2">{{> "icons/flame"}}</span>     ← colour and size come from the text
		{{{{/code}}}}
		<p><strong>Adding one:</strong> put its <a href="https://lucide.dev/icons/">Lucide</a> name in the <code>ICONS</code> list in <code>scripts/vendor.mjs</code> and run <code>npm run vendor</code>. Line icons are Lucide (ISC licence); <code>brand-*</code> marks are Simple Icons (CC0) and remain trademarks of their owners — use them only to link to that service. LinkedIn is not in Simple Icons, at LinkedIn's request, so <code>brand-linkedin</code> falls back to a neutral link icon.</p>
	</div>
</section>
